12. Demonstrate Error Handling
A good demonstration should also show that the system handles failures.

Possible examples:

Invalid Input
     ↓
Validation Message

or:

Gemini Unavailable
     ↓
Friendly Error Message
     ↓
Retry

This demonstrates that the application isn't dependent on an ideal successful response every time.

13. Suggested Presentation Script
You can use this during your viva/project demonstration:

"Good morning. Our project is FitBuddy-AI, an AI-powered fitness plan generator using Gemini models. The purpose of this system is to provide personalized workout plans based on the user's fitness goals, experience level, available equipment, training schedule, and preferred workout duration."

"First, the user logs into the application and completes a fitness assessment. These details are sent securely to our backend, which prepares a request for the Gemini model. Gemini generates a structured workout plan containing workout days, exercises, sets, repetitions, rest periods, and progression guidance."

"The generated plan is then validated and displayed on the user's dashboard. The user can view individual exercises, complete workouts, and request alternatives when an exercise is unsuitable or unavailable."

"The application also records completed workouts and presents the user's activity through the progress dashboard. This demonstrates how generative AI can be integrated with conventional application logic and database functionality to create a personalized fitness experience."

14. Questions the Evaluator May Ask
Why did you use Gemini?
Answer:

"Gemini provides generative AI capabilities that allow the application to create personalized workout plans from natural-language and structured user requirements rather than relying entirely on predefined routines."

Why use structured output?
"Structured output makes the AI response predictable and easier for the application to validate and render."

What happens if Gemini returns invalid data?
"The backend validates the response against the expected schema. Invalid responses are rejected or handled through an error/retry mechanism."

Is Gemini responsible for storing user data?
"No. User profiles, workout plans, and completion history are handled by the application's backend and database. Gemini is primarily used for AI generation and adaptation."

Can the AI replace a professional trainer or doctor?
"No. FitBuddy-AI is an AI-assisted fitness planning application. It should not be treated as a substitute for qualified professional medical or fitness advice, particularly when a user has an injury or medical condition."

What is the main advantage of the system?
"The main advantage is personalization. The generated plan can take the user's goals, experience, available equipment, schedule, and duration into account."

